# Gaming Overlay

- Separate simulation from rendering. Simulation runs on a fixed timestep; rendering interpolates.
- Multiplayer: the server is authoritative. Clients send inputs, not state. Validate every input (rate, range, cooldown).
- Keep simulation deterministic where replays or rollback are needed: seeded RNG, no wall-clock reads, stable iteration order.
- No allocations in per-frame hot paths. Pool frequently spawned objects (projectiles, particles, UI items).
- Define frame, memory, and asset budgets up front (e.g. 16.6 ms/frame at 60 fps) and keep them in config, not in code comments.
- Data-driven content: stats, levels, and balance live in versioned data files, not hardcoded.
- Save data is versioned with explicit migrations. Never break old saves silently.
- Input goes through an action-mapping layer (rebindable, gamepad/touch/keyboard), never raw device checks in gameplay code.
- Telemetry: batch events and persist offline (see telemetry rule); never emit per-frame events.
